---
import BrandHead from '../components/BrandHead.astro';
import MarketingFooter from '../components/marketing/MarketingFooter.astro';
import MarketingHeader from '../components/marketing/MarketingHeader.astro';
import { fluxzeroBrand } from '../config/brand.mjs';

const comparisonRows = [
    {
        label: 'Built for',
        values: [
            { status: 'Developers', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'Developers', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'Anyone building with AI', kind: 'included' },
        ],
    },
    {
        label: 'What you set up',
        values: [
            { status: 'Database, frontend hosting, permissions & integrations', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'Services, databases, networking, load balancing & deployment', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'No infrastructure setup', kind: 'included' },
        ],
    },
    {
        label: 'What the cloud handles',
        values: [
            { status: 'Auth, database & frontend hosting', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'Deployments, networking & databases', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'Everything your product needs to run', kind: 'included' },
        ],
    },
    {
        label: 'When you add a feature',
        values: [
            { status: 'Build the feature across every application layer', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'Build the feature across services and infrastructure', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'Define what the feature does', kind: 'included' },
        ],
    },
    {
        label: 'Security & recovery',
        values: [
            { status: 'Database backups; application recovery is left to you', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'Left for you to build into the application', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'Handled by the cloud', kind: 'included' },
        ],
    },
    {
        label: 'Path to scale',
        values: [
            { status: 'Requires rearchitecting or replatforming', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'Requires rearchitecting or replatforming', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'Scale without rebuilding', kind: 'included' },
        ],
    },
    {
        label: 'Based in',
        values: [
            { status: 'Singapore + United States', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'United States', kind: 'owned' },
            { status: 'European Union', kind: 'included' },
        ],
    },
];

const comparisonOptions = [
    {
        name: 'Supabase + Vercel',
        sub: 'Database platform + frontend cloud',
        index: 0,
    },
    {
        name: 'Railway',
        sub: 'Application infrastructure',
        index: 1,
    },
    {
        name: 'Fluxzero',
        sub: 'The product cloud',
        index: 2,
        featured: true,
    },
];

const homepageFaqs = [
    {
        question: 'What is Fluxzero?',
        answer: [
            'Fluxzero is a cloud platform for applications built with AI. It hosts your frontend and backend, stores your data, and runs the application in production.',
            'Unlike other clouds, Fluxzero gives every product a reliable backend, so your agent can focus on the product instead of its tech stack.',
        ],
    },
    {
        question: 'Can I really launch serious software with Fluxzero?',
        answer: [
            'Yes. Fluxzero is built for products where reliability matters: products with valuable data, complex workflows, permissions, integrations, and business rules.',
            'You and your coding agent build the product behavior. Fluxzero takes responsibility for the technical foundation underneath your product, including security, reliable message delivery, recovery, auditability, and scale.',
            'The same hardened foundation supports early-stage products and high-throughput enterprise workloads, so you can launch without hiring backend engineers and keep the same backend as your product grows.',
        ],
    },
    {
        question: 'My agent can generate a backend. Why should it use Fluxzero?',
        answer: [
            'An agent can generate a backend quickly. But building your product is a different job from building a hardened backend. Your agent is focused on the product. The backend it generates becomes a codebase you must keep secure, reliable, understandable, and ready to scale as the product evolves. Every shortcut taken to launch becomes something you own.',
            'Fluxzero gives your product a hardened backend foundation built and operated by experienced backend engineers for demanding enterprise workloads. Because products run on a shared platform foundation, improvements to security, reliability, recovery, and scale compound and benefit every product, without adding infrastructure code to your application.',
            'Your codebase stays focused on the product. As usage and complexity increase, you keep building on the same foundation instead of rebuilding or replatforming.',
        ],
    },
    {
        question: 'How is Fluxzero different from Supabase + Vercel, Railway, or other clouds?',
        answer: [
            'Those clouds give you infrastructure and services that still need to be selected, connected, secured, scaled, and operated. You or your agent remains responsible for turning them into one reliable product.',
            'Fluxzero provides and operates that application foundation as one cloud, so you can focus on the product instead of operating the platform underneath it. If you prefer to design, tune, and operate every infrastructure layer yourself, a component cloud may suit you better.',
        ],
    },
    {
        question: 'What does building with Fluxzero look like?',
        answer: [
            'Start by copying one instruction into your coding agent. This is the easiest way to build with Fluxzero. The application your agent helps you build is real code that developers can inspect, test, and extend from their own IDE. When the product is ready, the same application can be deployed to Fluxzero Cloud.',
        ],
    },
    {
        question: 'What kinds of products can I build?',
        answer: [
            'Any application can run on Fluxzero, across product domains and workload sizes. That includes SaaS products, marketplaces, portals, internal tools, consumer apps, and AI-enabled software.',
        ],
    },
    {
        question: 'What kinds of companies run on Fluxzero?',
        answer: [
            'Fluxzero is trusted in production across product domains and workload sizes, from single-founder companies and scale-ups to enterprises such as the organization behind the digital infrastructure of Europe\'s largest port.',
        ],
    },
    {
        question: 'Will I outgrow Fluxzero or need to rebuild later?',
        answer: [
            'No. The same application works locally and at production scale. Individual workloads can receive more capacity as your product grows, without forcing the whole product onto a new architecture.',
            'If developers join later, they work in a real codebase, not a generated black box. They can inspect, test, and extend the product in their own IDE while Fluxzero continues to run the foundation.',
        ],
    },
    {
        question: 'Do I lose visibility by trusting my backend to Fluxzero?',
        answer: [
            'No. Fluxzero is not a black box. It works more like an X-ray of your product: you can see its messages, web requests, application logs, errors, and the user or system behind each interaction.',
            'Every interaction is part of a searchable audit trail. Correlation and tracing let you follow a single request across applications or zoom out to find patterns, performance issues, and failures across the whole product.',
        ],
    },
    {
        question: 'Do I own my code and data?',
        answer: [
            'Yes. Your application code and product data remain yours. The code does not depend on proprietary Fluxzero annotations, and your data can be exported in a machine-readable format.',
        ],
    },
    {
        question: 'When do I start paying?',
        answer: [
            'Building and running locally is free. You start paying when you activate a plan to put your product online.',
        ],
    },
];

const homepageFaqSchema = {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: homepageFaqs.map((faq) => ({
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: faq.question,
        acceptedAnswer: {
            '@type': 'Answer',
            text: faq.answer.join('\n\n'),
        },
    })),
};
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <BrandHead title="Fluxzero — The European cloud for AI-built apps" description="Fluxzero is the European application cloud for people and AI agents building, running, and scaling real software." />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,wght@1,200;1,300;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/home.css?v=20260904-14">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/v4-home.css?v=20260905-1">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/marketing-shell.css?v=20260903-1">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(homepageFaqSchema)}></script>
</head>
<body class="v4-home">
<MarketingHeader />

<!-- 1 · HERO -->
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="hero-bg" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="hero-bg-core">
      <div class="hero-bg-radial"></div>
      <div class="hero-bg-ellipse"></div>
      <div class="hero-bg-base"></div>
      <div class="hero-bg-fade">
        <div class="hero-bg-fade-left"></div>
        <div class="hero-bg-fade-right"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-mobile-logo" aria-hidden="true">
      <img class="hero-logo-lockup" src={fluxzeroBrand.logo} width="181" height="40" alt="">
  </div>
  <h1 class="rv d1" id="hero-title"><span class="hero-title-main">The European cloud</span><br><span class="em">for AI-built apps</span></h1>

    <p class="hero-sub rv d2">
        The all-in-one cloud with frontend, backend, data, security, deployment, and observability working as one.
    </p>

    <div class="hero-ctas rv d3">
        <a href="/get-started" class="btn-p">Get started →</a>
        <a href="/contact#contactForm" class="btn-s">Talk to us</a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-signals rv d4" aria-label="European operation">
        <p class="hero-signal hero-signal--eu">
            <span class="hero-eu-stars" aria-hidden="true">
                {Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, index) => <span style={`--star:${index}`}>★</span>)}
            </span>
            <span>100% EU-operated · Built on ISO 27001-certified and SOC 2 Type 2-audited infrastructure.</span>
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="facts facts-carded rv section-stack" id="production-gap-content" aria-labelledby="production-gap-content-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 class="facts-heading h2-two-line" id="production-gap-content-title">The cloud for anyone</h2>
        <p class="facts-sub"><span>AI lets anyone build products.</span><br>Fluxzero gives every product a reliable backend from the first&nbsp;prompt.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="facts-g section-grid">
        <div class="fc">
            <div class="fc-head">
                <h4>Ship without an engineering team</h4>
            </div>
            <p>Build and launch serious products without assembling a backend or platform team.</p>
            <div class="fc-visual pg-demo-visual" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 280 150">
                    <text class="pg-label" x="24" y="34">BUILT</text>
                    <text class="pg-label" x="102" y="112">WORKING</text>
                    <text class="pg-label" x="208" y="34">LAUNCHED</text>
                    <path class="pg-path" d="M34 74 C88 40 112 100 142 74 S202 42 236 74"/>
                    <path class="pg-path--active" d="M34 74 C88 40 112 100 142 74 S202 42 236 74"/>
                    <circle class="pg-node" cx="34" cy="74" r="9"/>
                    <circle class="pg-node" cx="142" cy="74" r="9"/>
                    <circle class="pg-node pg-node--live" cx="236" cy="74" r="13"/>
                    <path class="pg-check pg-check--small" d="m30 73 3 3 6-7"/>
                    <path class="pg-check pg-check--small" d="m138 73 3 3 6-7"/>
                    <path class="pg-check" d="m230 74 4 4 8-9"/>
                </svg>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fc">
            <div class="fc-head">
                <h4>Build with peace of mind</h4>
            </div>
            <p>Security, reliability, and recovery are built in from day one, not left for you or your agent to get right.</p>
            <div class="fc-visual pg-guard-visual" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 280 150">
                    <circle class="pg-guard-aura pg-guard-aura--outer" cx="140" cy="72" r="55"/>
                    <circle class="pg-guard-aura pg-guard-aura--inner" cx="140" cy="72" r="41"/>

                    <g class="pg-guard-node pg-guard-node--security" transform="translate(140 23)">
                        <circle class="pg-guard-node-ring" r="6"/>
                        <path d="m-2.5 0 1.8 1.8 3.6-4"/>
                    </g>
                    <g class="pg-guard-node pg-guard-node--reliability" transform="translate(96 96)">
                        <circle class="pg-guard-node-ring" r="6"/>
                        <path d="m-2.5 0 1.8 1.8 3.6-4"/>
                    </g>
                    <g class="pg-guard-node pg-guard-node--recovery" transform="translate(184 96)">
                        <circle class="pg-guard-node-ring" r="6"/>
                        <path d="m-2.5 0 1.8 1.8 3.6-4"/>
                    </g>

                    <path class="pg-guard-shield" d="m140 44 27 10v16c0 15-11 28-27 35-16-7-27-20-27-35V54l27-10Z"/>
                    <path class="pg-guard-check" d="m130 72 7 7 14-16"/>
                </svg>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fc">
            <div class="fc-head">
                <h4>Scale without replatforming</h4>
            </div>
            <p>The same application model works locally and at full scale, so growth does not force a new architecture.</p>
            <div class="fc-visual pg-business-visual" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 280 142">
                    <path class="pg-business-grid" d="M28 116 H244 M28 88 H244 M28 60 H244 M28 32 H244 M64 20 V116 M112 20 V116 M160 20 V116 M208 20 V116"/>
                    <path class="pg-business-arrow-glow" d="M32 108 L74 90 L104 98 L140 66 L172 76 L226 30"/>
                    <path class="pg-business-arrow" d="M32 108 L74 90 L104 98 L140 66 L172 76 L226 30"/>
                    <path class="pg-business-arrow-head" d="M244 14 L233 38 L219 21 Z"/>
                    <circle class="pg-business-spark" cx="74" cy="90" r="2.2"/>
                    <circle class="pg-business-spark" cx="140" cy="66" r="2.2"/>
                    <text class="pg-business-label" x="24" y="128">IDEA</text>
                    <text class="pg-business-label" x="114" y="128">USERS</text>
                    <text class="pg-business-label" x="202" y="128">BUSINESS</text>
                </svg>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>


<section class="comparison comparison-v4 rv section-stack" id="platform-comparison" aria-labelledby="comparison-title">
    <div class="section-intro comparison-v4__heading">
        <h2 class="h2-two-line" id="comparison-title">Other clouds run infrastructure.<br><span>Fluxzero runs your product.</span></h2>
        <p>Infrastructure clouds leave you responsible for the tech stack.<br>With Fluxzero, your only responsibility is the product.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="comparison-desktop section-grid" role="table" aria-label="Comparison of application cloud approaches">
        <div class="comparison-head" role="row">
            <div class="comparison-head__corner" role="columnheader" aria-label="Comparison category"></div>
            {comparisonOptions.map((option) => (
                <div class:list={['comparison-head__option', { 'is-featured': option.featured }]} role="columnheader">
                    <h3>{option.name}</h3>
                    <p>{option.sub}</p>
                </div>
            ))}
        </div>
        <div class="comparison-table" role="rowgroup">
            {comparisonRows.map((row) => (
                <div class="comparison-table__row" role="row">
                    <div class="comparison-table__label" role="rowheader">{row.label}</div>
                    {comparisonOptions.map((option) => {
                        const value = row.values[option.index];
                        return (
                            <div class:list={['comparison-table__cell', { 'is-featured': option.featured }]} role="cell">
                                <span class:list={['comparison-table__mark', `is-${value.kind}`]} aria-hidden="true">
                                    {value.kind === 'included' ? '✓' : '—'}
                                </span>
                                <strong>{value.status}</strong>
                            </div>
                        );
                    })}
                </div>
            ))}
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="comparison-mobile section-grid">
        {comparisonOptions.map((option) => (
            <details class:list={['comparison-disclosure', { 'is-featured': option.featured }]} open={option.featured}>
                <summary>
                    <span>
                        <strong>{option.name}</strong>
                        <small>{option.sub}</small>
                    </span>
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 8 5 5 5-5"/></svg>
                </summary>
                <div class="comparison-disclosure__body">
                    <dl>
                        {comparisonRows.map((row) => (
                            <>
                                <dt>{row.label}</dt>
                                <dd>
                                    <span class:list={['comparison-table__mark', `is-${row.values[option.index].kind}`]} aria-hidden="true">
                                        {row.values[option.index].kind === 'included' ? '✓' : '—'}
                                    </span>
                                    <strong>{row.values[option.index].status}</strong>
                                </dd>
                            </>
                        ))}
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </details>
        ))}
    </div>

    <div class="comparison-v4__actions">
        <a class="btn-s" href="/how-it-works">Explore how Fluxzero works →</a>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="sp"></div>

<!-- 4 · AI -->
<section class="ai rv section-stack" id="ai-works-better" aria-labelledby="ai-works-better-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="ai-eyebrow">No technical noise</p>
        <h2 class="h2-two-line" id="ai-works-better-title"><span class="ai-line-1">AI works better</span><span class="ai-line-2">when there&rsquo;s less to think about</span></h2>

        <p class="ai-body">
            When AI does not have to integrate cloud infrastructure, it can stay focused on the product behavior you actually care about.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-points section-grid">
        <div class="ai-pt">
            <h4>
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path d="M5 7.5h14M5 12h10M5 16.5h7" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                    <path d="m16 16.5 2 2 4-5" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                </svg>
                Spend fewer tokens
            </h4>
            <p>Spend your prompt budget on product behavior, features, and user experience.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ai-pt">
            <h4>
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path d="M12 3.7 18.2 6v5.2c0 4.1-2.5 7.6-6.2 9.1-3.7-1.5-6.2-5-6.2-9.1V6L12 3.7Z" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                    <path d="m9.2 12.1 1.9 1.9 3.9-4.3" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                </svg>
                Less risk
            </h4>
            <p>Infrastructure is no longer your AI agent’s responsibility.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ai-pt">
            <h4>
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path d="m8 9-3 3 3 3" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                    <path d="m16 9 3 3-3 3" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                    <path d="m10.5 16.5 3-9" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                </svg>
                100% product context
            </h4>
            <p>The tech stack no longer consumes your agent&rsquo;s context, so every prompt can stay focused on the product.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="sp"></div>


<!-- 8 · PROOF -->
<section class="proof rv section-stack" id="proven-foundation" aria-labelledby="proven-foundation-title">
    <div class="proof-label">Built to scale</div>
    <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 class="h2-single" id="proven-foundation-title">Start small.<br>Scale as your product grows.</h2>
        <div class="proof-body">
            <p>The same foundation supports early products<br class="desktop-break"> and high-throughput systems with complex business logic.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="proof-stats section-grid" data-proof-stats>
        <dl class="proof-stat">
            <dt class="label">GB / min production throughput</dt>
            <dd class="num"><span class="proof-count" data-count-to="100">100</span><span>+</span></dd>
            <dd class="proof-stat__context">About 700,000 tweets every second, nearly 5 times X.com&rsquo;s record.<sup><a href="#tweet-throughput-note" aria-label="How this estimate was calculated">*</a></sup></dd>
        </dl>
        <dl class="proof-stat">
            <dt class="label">resolved requests / sec</dt>
            <dd class="num"><span class="proof-count" data-count-to="1">1</span><span>M+</span></dd>
            <dd class="proof-stat__context">Commands and results, end to end across applications.</dd>
        </dl>
        <dl class="proof-stat">
            <dt class="label">less application code</dt>
            <dd class="num"><small>up to</small> <span class="proof-count" data-count-to="99">99</span><span>%</span></dd>
            <dd class="proof-stat__context">Across legacy migrations with the same behavior.</dd>
        </dl>
    </div>

    <p class="proof-source" id="tweet-throughput-note">
        * Estimate based on a <a href="https://www.research-collection.ethz.ch/bitstreams/77b38ad3-f165-4bda-9fca-6a1d13913836/download" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2.3 kB average serialized tweet size</a> and <a href="https://blog.x.com/engineering/en_us/a/2013/new-tweets-per-second-record-and-how" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">X.com&rsquo;s published record of 143,199 tweets per second</a>.
    </p>

</section>

<div class="sp"></div>

<!-- 9 · FAQ -->
<section class="faq rv section-stack" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 class="faq-heading h2-single" id="faq-title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list section-grid">
        {homepageFaqs.map((faq, index) => {
            const answerId = `homepage-faq-answer-${index + 1}`;

            return (
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <h3 class="faq-question-heading">
                        <button class="faq-q" type="button" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls={answerId}>
                            <span>{faq.question}</span>
                            <span class="faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                        </button>
                    </h3>
                    <div class="faq-a" id={answerId}>
                        {faq.answer.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
                    </div>
                </div>
            );
        })}
    </div>

    <p class="faq-help">Still wondering? <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a> and we'll help.</p>
</section>

<section class="cta-end rv" aria-labelledby="cta-end-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="cta-end-title">
            <span class="cta-title-main">Launch what used to require</span>
            <span class="cta-title-accent">an entire engineering team.</span>
        </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-btns">
        <a href="/get-started" class="btn-p">Get started →</a>
        <a href="/contact#contactForm" class="btn-s">Talk to us</a>
    </div>
</section>

<MarketingFooter />

    <script src="/js/home.js?v=20260904-2" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
